@meta
id: 25-12
title: Drill — a comma on every line
chapter: 25
type: drill
skills: ex-normal
par: 21
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: Alt-click six line ends, type one comma
open: skus.ts

@brief
Eight times: the six sku strings on lines 2 to 7 have lost their trailing
commas. Put them back with one command. The brackets on lines 1 and 8
must not get one.

@keys
| `:2,7normal A,` | press `A,` on lines 2 to 7 |

@hints
Range first, then `normal`, then the two keys you would have pressed on
one line.
--
`:2,7normal A,` Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :2,7normal A,<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Eighteen keystrokes. The habit being drilled is the order you build the
command in: decide the keys for one line, then put a range in front of
them. People who learn it the other way round end up staring at a half
typed `:2,7` wondering what they were going to do with it.

Numeric ranges are fine when the block is on screen and the gutter is
right there. Everything you learned in the first half of this chapter
still applies — `:/\[/+1,/]/-1normal A,` is the version that does not
care what line the array starts on.

@start skus.ts
export const skus = [
  'sku_101'
  'sku_102'
  'sku_103'
  'sku_104'
  'sku_105'
  'sku_106'
];

@expected skus.ts
export const skus = [
  'sku_101',
  'sku_102',
  'sku_103',
  'sku_104',
  'sku_105',
  'sku_106',
];
